x86/intel: keep fast strings in a guest

The boot clears REP_GOOD and ERMS when IA32_MISC_ENABLE has no fast
string bit. In a guest the MSR is the value of the VMM (KVM gives 0
for the bit), and the CPU runs the string instructions with the
setting of the host. The check is now skipped in a guest, so memcpy,
memset, and the clear of a page use rep movs and rep stos.

Measured on KVM, 1 CPU, 64 MB, root on dm-verity: the start of init
is 0.05 ms (best) to 0.4 ms (mean of 8) earlier.

--- a/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/intel.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kernel/cpu/intel.c
@@ -328,8 +328,12 @@
 	/*
 	 * If fast string is not enabled in IA32_MISC_ENABLE for any reason,
 	 * clear the fast string and enhanced fast string CPU capabilities.
+	 * A guest skips the check: its IA32_MISC_ENABLE is the value that
+	 * the VMM gives, and the CPU runs the string instructions of the
+	 * guest with the setting of the host.
 	 */
-	if (c->x86 > 6 || (c->x86 == 6 && c->x86_model >= 0xd)) {
+	if (!cpu_has(c, X86_FEATURE_HYPERVISOR) &&
+	    (c->x86 > 6 || (c->x86 == 6 && c->x86_model >= 0xd))) {
 		rdmsrl(MSR_IA32_MISC_ENABLE, misc_enable);
 		if (!(misc_enable & MSR_IA32_MISC_ENABLE_FAST_STRING)) {
 			pr_info("Disabled fast string operations\n");
